        "title": "Coral Biology: Polyp Anatomy, Skeleton, Spawning, Growth",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Coral is an animal — phylum Cnidaria, class Anthozoa. Each coral \"head\" is a colony of genetically identical polyps sharing a basal tissue layer (coenosarc) and a communal skeleton. The polyp is a simple sac-like animal but its capacity to precision-engineer an aragonite skeleton, maintain an endosymbiosis, and coordinate colonial growth makes it the architect of the ocean's most structurally complex habitat."
